  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most important first step is to establish a clean, reliable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the space: it uses PCA (a deterministic, low-failure-risk encoder) on a single RNA profile with no image, aggregation, or fusion. This gives a well-defined reference accuracy for the RNA signal alone. From this baseline, I can then measure the marginal contribution of (a) better RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt), (b) multiprofile + aggregation, (c) the image modality, and (d) multimodal fusion. Starting with the simplest, most interpretable configuration reduces uncertainty about the floor performance and prevents conflating multiple design choices in the first experiment. Under a 10-experiment budget, anchoring to a simple baseline before exploring complexity is the most information-efficient use of experiment 1."
}

